WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:01.768
It was

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.236
quite a day on the Hill yesterday.

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.070
Attorney General Merrick

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.305
Garland tackled

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:06.306
more than 4 hours

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:07.474
of questioning by the Senate

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:08.241
Judiciary Committee.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.876
Republicans eager to press him

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.044
on the investigations

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.579
into President Biden

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:14.314
and Trump over classified documents.

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:16.349
On top of questions about Hunter Biden,

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.785
also questions about fentanyl,

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.987
the sale of deadly drugs and social media

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:22.422
and, of course,

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.691
the ticketing issues around

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.559
Taylor Swift's concert.

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.161
Paula Reid live for CNN

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.362
this morning in Washington.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:30.296
When I say that in jest,

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.198
but it's a really serious issue

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:34.701
about whether there's monopoly

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:35.268
power there.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:36.336
But what did you take away

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:37.670
from this hearing?

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:38.238
Exactly.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:38.905
And Ticketmaster

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:39.973
is also one area

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:42.542
where you can find bipartisan consensus.

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:44.577
But one of the biggest takeaways

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:45.712
from yesterday's hearing,

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:46.479
I mean, remember,

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:46.980
this is usually

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.548
a pretty contentious forum

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:49.449
that was really surprised

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.384
by how much substance was covered.

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:51.785
And they talked

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:52.752
about fentanyl,

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:55.255
violent crime and child labor.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.090
And it was really 4 hours

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:57.757
into the hearing

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.959
before any Republicans even asked

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:00.994
about the investigation

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:02.028
into former President Trump

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:05.799
You were the attorney general

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:07.534
of the United States.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.169
You are in charge

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:10.236
of the Justice Department.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.839
And yes, sir, you are responsible.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:14.441
So give me an answer.

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:15.542
Attorney General Merrick

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.010
Garland appeared on Capitol

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.011
Hill Wednesday

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.379
amid high profile

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:21.081
investigations into President

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:23.283
Biden and former President Trump

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:24.484
but warned

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:26.586
he would not be able to reveal details

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.621
of any ongoing cases

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:29.622
so that we do not

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:30.323
jeopardize

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.358
the viability of our investigations

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.894
and the civil liberties of our citizens.

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:37.097
Though
he was willing to explain why

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:39.199
he is not appointed a special counsel

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:40.633
to handle an investigation

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.135
into Hunter Biden,

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:44.170
I promised to leave the matter of Joe

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.638
Biden in the hands of the U.S.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:46.473
attorney

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.108
for the District of Delaware,

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:49.442
who was appointed

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.344
in the previous administration.

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:53.313
Yet after months of Republicans

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.981
railing against the FBI

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:57.283
for executing a search warrant

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.419
at Trump's Mar a Lago home,

00:01:59.419 --> 00:01:59.853
they didn't

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:00.753
bring that up

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:03.656
until 4 hours into the hearing.

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.225
I approved the decision

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:06.793
to seek a search warrant

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:07.594
after probable

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:08.928
cause was overruling

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:11.831
the FBI agent who did not want to do so.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:12.599
Garland

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.467
repeatedly defended the department

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.836
against accusations of Partizanship.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.438
They also want to at least respond

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:19.606
to their characterization

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:20.373
of the department,

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.742
which I vigorously disagree with.

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:23.877
I believe the men and women

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:24.878
of the department

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:25.945
pursue their work

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.414
every single day in a nonpartisan

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.883
and appropriate federal garland.

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:30.750
As Republicans

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:31.851
hammered the attorney

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:33.286
general on protests

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:35.522
at the homes of Supreme Court justices

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:36.890
and other conservative

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:39.092
causes, your failure to act

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:41.094
to protect the safety of the justices

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:42.529
and their families

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:45.331
was an obvious product of political bias.

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:48.101
Garland said his decision to have U.S.

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:50.103
marshals protect the justices.

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:52.639
20 47 was unprecedented.

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:54.007
Senator, you asked me

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:55.408
whether I sat on my hands

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:56.643
and quite the opposite.

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:58.211
I sent 70 United

00:02:58.211 --> 00:02:59.579
States marshals try again.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:01.681
Has the department

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.550
of Justice brought even a single case

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:04.184
under this statute?

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:05.218
So, yes, no question.

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:06.252
It's not a get

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:07.554
give a speech on the other things

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:08.188
you did.

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:09.556
The job of the United States

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:11.291
Marshals is to defend the lives.

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:12.258
The answer is no.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:14.427
It said defend the lives of the justices.

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:16.429
And that's their number one priority.

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:19.032
Garland also engaged on a controversy

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:19.966
that unites

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:21.167
even the staunchest

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:22.869
political adversaries.

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:25.471
Ticketmaster multiple lawmakers

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.873
brought up the Justice Department's

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:29.042
reported antitrust investigation

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:31.411
into Ticketmaster's parent company.

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.612
Following the botched

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:35.014
handling of Taylor Swift concerts.

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:36.349
We know, quote,

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:37.450
all too well, close

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:38.184
quote,

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:39.619
the importance of competition

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:41.421
in this industry.

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:44.290
As in all other industries.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:45.892
And so you can be confident

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:47.827
that in all of our work,

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:50.196
we approach you with an understanding

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:51.264
that highly Concentré

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.265
rated industries are

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:53.433
a problem for competition.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:56.703
Did you catch that?

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.271
I can confirm from conversations

00:03:58.271 --> 00:03:59.005
to the attorney general

00:03:59.005 --> 00:03:59.806
that he is actually

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:01.541
a big Taylor Swift fan.

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:02.041
Now, aside

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.043
from the distrust of Ticketmaster,

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:05.678
the other area where there was clear

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.914
bipartisan consensus was fentanyl

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:08.581
and the fact that we were

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:10.850
just not doing enough on that issue.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:11.284
And the attorney

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:12.952
general reminded lawmakers

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:15.154
that he can only work with the laws

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:16.022
and the resources

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:17.190
that he was given by Congress

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.158
and said he would welcome more help

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:19.859
on that issue.

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:21.527
It's great that you point out, too,

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:22.362
how much substance

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:23.596
there was in those hearings.

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:25.365
Right,
because that is critically important

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:26.132
for the American people.

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:26.866
It's what they deserve.

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:28.301
Paula, thank you for the reporting.

